{
  "board": { "name": "Ads Autopilot", "color": "#22D3EE" },
  "columns": [
    {
      "name": "Research",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Confirm Meta Marketing API access tiers & app-review requirements",
          "label": "api-access",
          "body": "Verify current state: new apps start on **Standard/Limited** access (own accounts only, ~60-pt quota); **Advanced/Full** needed to manage third-party clients (~9,000-pt quota). Advanced requires **App Review + Business Verification + screencast per permission + working client-onboarding flow + privacy policy**. Note 2026-05-04 rename of AMSA -> 'Marketing API Access Tier' (Limited vs Full). Capture required permissions: ads_management, ads_read, business_management. Source: developers.facebook.com/docs/marketing-api, singhamandeep.com app-review guide."
        },
        {
          "title": "Confirm Google Ads API developer-token levels & timeline",
          "label": "api-access",
          "body": "Per official docs: Test (test only, 15k ops/day) -> Explorer (prod 2,880 ops/day) -> Basic (15k ops/day, ~5 biz-day review) -> Standard (unlimited most services, ~10 biz-day review). Token tied to **Manager/MCC account**, OAuth2 per client, Google Cloud project. Note 2026-07-07 brand-verification pilot can cut pending review to hours. Source: developers.google.com/google-ads/api/docs/access-levels."
        },
        {
          "title": "Confirm TikTok Marketing API approval path & limits",
          "label": "api-access",
          "body": "Path: dev registration -> app -> **Business Center onboarding** -> sandbox->prod app review -> business verification (higher volume) -> data-security audit. Basic ~3-7 biz days; advanced/high-volume 1-3 weeks; quota increases case-by-case, no self-serve, no SLA. v1.3 + OAuth. Rate: ~600 RPM/endpoint, 1-min sliding window, per-app/token/advertiser quotas. Source: soku.ai TikTok Marketing API v1.3, getphyllo rate limits."
        },
        {
          "title": "Build API capability matrix (CRUD/creative/insights) per platform",
          "label": "api-access",
          "body": "Confirm each platform supports campaign/adset(group)/ad CRUD, budget get/set, creative upload (image/video), insights/reporting, audiences. Google adds mutate ops + GAQL + recommendations. Document endpoint names, versioning cadence (Google v23.x), and pagination. Feeds the unified data model."
        },
        {
          "title": "Competitor teardown: Madgicx / Revealbot / AdEspresso / Smartly / Metadata",
          "label": "market",
          "body": "Madgicx ~$49/mo Meta-only AI; Revealbot ~$99/mo cross-platform rules; AdEspresso ~$49/mo SMB split-testing; Smartly enterprise (~$5k/mo floor, ~$90k median annual); Metadata B2B custom (~$60k reports). **Gap = Revealbot-class cross-platform automation + built-in AI creative at SMB/agency pricing, bundled with Nxeon.** Sources: admanage.ai, adlibrary.com, get-ryze.ai."
        },
        {
          "title": "Research budget-pacing math & overspend guardrails",
          "label": "research",
          "body": "Target curve = target_spend x (elapsed/total) with dayparting weights; pace_ratio = actual/expected each tick. Respect platform realities: Google spends up to **2x daily / 30.4x monthly**. Overspend guard = project month-end spend, auto-pause when > cap. Source: get-ryze.ai Google pacing formula, wevion.ai FB pacing."
        },
        {
          "title": "Research rules-engine patterns & safety guardrails",
          "label": "research",
          "body": "Condition tree (AND/OR of metric comparisons over lookback) + action + schedule + guardrails. Must-haves: min-impressions/significance floor, cooldown per entity, max daily budget change, global kill-switch, insights-freshness gate, dry-run mode. Example rule pattern captured in architecture.md."
        },
        {
          "title": "Research compliance: Meta/Google/TikTok policy + PII handling",
          "label": "compliance",
          "body": "Meta Platform Terms: ad data must NOT be combined with PII to identify users, nor used outside stated functions. Support auto-pause of Rejected/Limited ads; flag sensitive verticals (health/politics/finance). Encrypted token vault, data-retention policy, GDPR/consent for audiences, per-tenant isolation, full audit log. Sources: adamigo.ai compliance/GDPR, adsuploader.com guidelines."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Ideas",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "AI creative generation via existing Nxeon tooling",
          "label": "creative",
          "body": "Do NOT rebuild image/copy generation. Reuse Nxeon's ad-creative tooling to produce image/video/copy variants, store as Creative(source=ai_generated, nxeon_asset_ref), then upload to platforms and feed into rotation/testing. Key differentiator vs Revealbot."
        },
        {
          "title": "Nxeon bundle upsell — ads where the site already lives",
          "label": "growth",
          "body": "Position for existing Nxeon hosting/marketing customers: manage paid ads in the same portal as their site + creatives. One login, one bill, unified brand assets. Lower CAC via existing base."
        },
        {
          "title": "Natural-language campaign builder / autopilot agent",
          "label": "ai",
          "body": "Metadata.io markets AI agents that build audiences, generate creative, set budgets, and launch from one prompt. Explore a later NL layer over our rules + creative engine. Backlog/Later, not Phase 1."
        },
        {
          "title": "Creative-fatigue detection & auto-rotation",
          "label": "creative",
          "body": "Detect rising frequency / falling CTR per creative; auto-retire fatigued creatives and promote AI-generated replacements. Ties rules engine + creative library + Nxeon generation."
        },
        {
          "title": "Anomaly alerts & burn-down notifications via Nxeon",
          "label": "reporting",
          "body": "Push spend-spike, pacing-off-target, and ad-rejection alerts through Nxeon's notification/email system. Client-facing exportable PDF/CSV reports."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Backlog",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Design unified Prisma data model",
          "label": "architecture",
          "body": "Organization -> AdAccountConnection(platform enum, enc tokens) -> Campaign -> AdSet(AdGroup) -> Ad -> Creative. Plus InsightSnapshot (daily fact table), Rule, RuleExecution, BudgetPlan, AuditLog. Canonical metrics + raw JSONB for platform extras; store currency + timezone per account. See architecture.md section 5."
        },
        {
          "title": "Design framework-agnostic core package (@ads-autopilot/core)",
          "label": "architecture",
          "body": "Platform clients + data model + rules engine + pacing + sync workers live in a core package that neither UI depends on directly, so standalone app and Nxeon /admin/ads add-on both import it. Enables the dual-ship requirement."
        },
        {
          "title": "OAuth + encrypted token vault + refresh worker",
          "label": "security",
          "body": "Per-client OAuth for all three platforms; least-scope; store tokens encrypted (KMS or libsodium-sealed columns); background auto-refresh; rotation. Never log tokens."
        },
        {
          "title": "Centralized rate-limiter respecting 3 quota models",
          "label": "architecture",
          "body": "Token-bucket per platform + per ad account: Meta BUC points (separate insights vs management pools, 100 POST/sec hard cap), Google ops/day, TikTok RPM sliding window. Batch mutations; cache insights; never hit live APIs on dashboard load."
        },
        {
          "title": "Durable job queue + scheduler for sync/pacing/rules ticks",
          "label": "architecture",
          "body": "BullMQ+Redis or pg-boss (Postgres-native). Periodic evaluation ticks (15-60 min) for rules + pacing; incremental insight syncs (hourly for pacing-critical accounts). Idempotent jobs, retries, dead-letter."
        },
        {
          "title": "Unified reporting metric-mapping spec",
          "label": "reporting",
          "body": "Normalize spend/impressions/clicks/CTR/CPM/CPC/conversions/CPA/revenue/ROAS across platforms with documented mapping; label differing attribution windows explicitly. Cache aggregates."
        },
        {
          "title": "Legal: privacy policy, ToS, data-handling doc, screencast demo",
          "label": "compliance",
          "body": "Required artifacts for Meta App Review + Google/TikTok reviews: public privacy policy, ToS, data-retention/PII doc, and a working client-onboarding demo + per-permission screencast. Blocks Advanced access."
        },
        {
          "title": "Multi-tenant client-onboarding flow",
          "label": "product",
          "body": "The mechanism by which a third-party business grants the app access to their ad accounts — required to demonstrate the client-facing use case for Meta ads_management Advanced access. Per-org data isolation."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Phase 1",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Submit all 3 API access applications (Day 1, parallel)",
          "label": "api-access",
          "body": "LONG POLE — start immediately. Meta: create app, submit Business Verification + App Review. Google: apply dev token (use test account meanwhile), set up MCC. TikTok: Business Center onboarding + app review. Budget 4-8 weeks calendar; build read-only on own accounts while pending."
        },
        {
          "title": "Scaffold core package + Prisma schema + Postgres",
          "label": "build",
          "body": "Implement the unified data model from Backlog as @ads-autopilot/core with Prisma; migrations; Postgres on dev box 51.79.226.215. Framework-agnostic; no UI coupling."
        },
        {
          "title": "Meta OAuth + account/campaign/insight read-only sync",
          "label": "build",
          "body": "Works under Standard/Limited access on own accounts. Connect Meta, discover ad accounts, sync campaigns/adsets/ads + daily InsightSnapshots into unified schema. Proves the model before write ops."
        },
        {
          "title": "Nxeon /admin/ads module shell (feature-flagged)",
          "label": "build",
          "body": "Mount add-on under /admin/ads reusing Nxeon auth/org/notifications; import @ads-autopilot/core. Gate behind ENABLE_ADS_AUTOPILOT until API access + security review pass. Match Nxeon theme (cyan #22D3EE)."
        },
        {
          "title": "Unified reporting dashboard v1 (Meta only)",
          "label": "build",
          "body": "Cross-platform-ready dashboard rendering the canonical metric set from InsightSnapshot: overview, per-account drilldown, creative leaderboard, spend burn-down. Reads cached aggregates only."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Later",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Google Ads connector (GAQL sync + mutate)",
          "label": "build",
          "body": "Add Google under same schema once Basic access clears. GAQL reporting, mutate ops for campaigns/adgroups/ads/budgets, recommendations. Use Opteo google-ads-api lib; version-pin (v23.x cadence)."
        },
        {
          "title": "TikTok connector (v1.3 sync + campaign ops)",
          "label": "build",
          "body": "Add TikTok under same schema once app review clears. Campaign management, reporting, audiences. Centralized RPM pacing."
        },
        {
          "title": "Write-ops mutation layer + audit log",
          "label": "build",
          "body": "Pause/enable, budget/bid adjust, creative rotate across all platforms. Every mutation writes AuditLog(before/after + platform_response). Idempotent; dry-run mode first."
        },
        {
          "title": "Rules engine + scheduler + guardrails",
          "label": "build",
          "body": "Condition tree evaluator over lookback windows, actions, schedules. Guardrails: significance floor, cooldown, max daily budget change, kill-switch, insights-freshness gate. RuleExecution logging."
        },
        {
          "title": "Budget-pacing engine + dayparting + overspend guard",
          "label": "build",
          "body": "Target-curve pacing with dayparting weights; throttle/raise budget by pace_ratio; hard monthly cap with projected-overspend auto-pause (accounts for Google 2x/30.4x behavior)."
        },
        {
          "title": "Creative rotation / A-B testing + AI generation hookup",
          "label": "creative",
          "body": "Rotate creatives, promote winners, retire fatigued ones; generate replacements via Nxeon ad-creative tooling; upload to platforms. Ties Creative library + rules engine."
        },
        {
          "title": "Multi-tenant billing + client reports + quota dashboards",
          "label": "product",
          "body": "Standalone SaaS billing (or Nxeon billing for add-on), exportable client-facing PDF/CSV reports, per-account API-quota/health dashboards, alert delivery."
        },
        {
          "title": "Standalone app deployment on dev box",
          "label": "devops",
          "body": "Own Next.js app + own Postgres on 51.79.226.215 with own auth/billing, sharing @ads-autopilot/core with the Nxeon add-on. Reversible migration between shared vs separate DB."
        },
        {
          "title": "NL autopilot agent layer (stretch)",
          "label": "ai",
          "body": "Natural-language layer over rules + pacing + creative: 'build audience, set budget, launch'. Only after core automation is proven and trusted. Stretch goal."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Done",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Initial research + architecture doc written",
          "label": "research",
          "body": "Completed 2026-08-10: product overview, competitor teardown, per-platform API access requirements + approval timelines + capabilities, tech stack, unified data model, rules/pacing design, reporting, dual-ship plan, phased roadmap, risks, compliance. See projects/ads/architecture.md with cited sources."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

